(Problem Context: A circular cross-section of radius r = 50 mm is revolved about a) Tj
T*
(non-intersecting coplanar axis at a distance R = 200 mm from the circle center to) Tj
T*
(generate a circular ring torus. Using the Pappus-Guldinus theorems, calculate: \(1\) Total) Tj
T*
(surface area of the torus, \(2\) Total volume enclosed.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Apply First Pappus-Guldinus Theorem for Surface Area:) Tj
T*
(Perimeter of generating circle: L = 2 * pi * r = 2 * pi * 50 = 314.16 mm.) Tj
T*
(Distance of curve centroid from axis of revolution: y_bar = R = 200 mm.) Tj
T*
(Distance traversed by centroid in one revolution: 2 * pi * y_bar = 2 * pi * 200 =) Tj
T*
(1256.64 mm.) Tj
T*
(Surface Area A = 2 * pi * R * L = \(2 * pi * 200\) * \(2 * pi * 50\) = 4 * pi^2 * R * r.) Tj
T*
(A = 4 * \(3.14159\)^2 * 200 * 50 = 39.4784 * 10,000 = 394,784 mm^2 = 0.395 m^2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Apply Second Pappus-Guldinus Theorem for Volume:) Tj
T*
(Area of generating circle: A_circle = pi * r^2 = pi * \(50\)^2 = 7853.98 mm^2.) Tj
T*
(Volume V = 2 * pi * R * A_circle = \(2 * pi * 200\) * \(pi * 50^2\) = 2 * pi^2 * R * r^2.) Tj
T*
(V = 2 * \(3.14159\)^2 * 200 * \(2500\) = 19.7392 * 500,000 = 9,869,604 mm^3 = 0.00987 m^3.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Total surface area A = 0.395 m^2, Total enclosed volume V = 0.00987 m^3.) Tj
